# Java Best Practices (From 15 Years Experience)

## Error Handling
Always use specific exceptions:
- ❌ `throw new RuntimeException("User not found")`
- ✅ `throw new UserNotFoundException(userId)`

## Logging
Log at appropriate levels:
- DEBUG: Development details, method entry/exit
- INFO: Major operations (user creation, order placed)
- WARN: Recoverable issues (retryable failures)
- ERROR: Unrecoverable issues requiring human intervention

## Null Safety
Use Optional for nullable values:
```java
// ❌
public String getEmail() {
    return email;
}

// ✅
public Optional<String> getEmail() {
    return Optional.ofNullable(email);
}